{"type": "message", "id": "aba95062", "parentId": "2d3dadb1", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T19:34:43.784Z", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "The task is complete. Let me summarize:\n\nThe quarters where Tesla reported quarterly data showing net profit margin percentages over 10.5% in 2023 are:\n- Q1 (10.88%)\n- Q4 (31.56%)\n\nQ2 was very close at 10.49% but did not exceed 10.5%.\nQ3 was well below at 8.04%.\n\nThe answer has been written to answer.txt.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning"}, {"type": "text", "text": "**Answer: Q1, Q4**\n\nBased on Tesla's SEC filings (10-Qs and 10-K) for 2023:\n\n- **Q1** (ended March 31, 2023): Net income $2,539M ÷ Revenue $23,329M = **10.88%** ✅\n- **Q2** (ended June 30, 2023): Net income $2,614M ÷ Revenue $24,927M = **10.49%** ❌\n- **Q3** (ended September 30, 2023): Net income $1,878M ÷ Revenue $23,350M = **8.04%** ❌\n- **Q4** (ended December 31, 2023): Net income $7,943M ÷ Revenue $25,167M = **31.56%** ✅\n\nNote: Q4's GAAP net income included a $5.9 billion one-time non-cash tax benefit, significantly inflating that quarter's margin."}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "openrouter", "model": "xiaomi/mimo-v2-omni", "usage": {"input": 686, "output": 471, "cacheRead": 57876, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 59033, "cost": {"input": 0.0002744, "output": 0.0009419999999999999, "cacheRead": 0.00463008, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.005846479999999999}}, "stopReason": "stop", "timestamp": 1775590480157, "responseId": "gen-1775590480-a2QlwcefQAbfprMqyVWq"}}
